=== WHAT WAS BUILT (parity with the web source, read end-to-end) ===
  LiveTelemetryPanels is the live-telemetry section of the Vehicle Detail page: a FadeIn
  "Live Telemetry" header with a pulsing live indicator, over a responsive 1-col→2-col grid
  of seven telemetry panels. The native surface reproduces its data, composition, every
  state, and i18n keys via shared P1/S8 state-holder seams (no view I/O):

  Composition (web → native), all SEVEN panels reproduced VERBATIM (not stubbed):
   1. Powertrain      — shift-state chip (D/R/N tones), the −300…+300 kW power bar,
                        front/rear rpm + torque MetricCard tiles, peak-motor (>80 °C danger)
                        + inverter temps, regen.
   2. Climate         — cabin/outside temp tiles, driver/passenger setpoints, HVAC state,
                        the 6-bar fan meter, defrost/climate/precondition mode chips.
   3. Security        — lock block (Locked/Unlocked), sentry chip, doors/windows/user-present
                        rows, detail line, remote-start access (web `hasData` = security OR
                        remoteStartEnabled present).
   4. Vehicle State   — high-beams / turn-signal / hazards, driver-seat / paired-keys,
                        valet / service / speed-limit / center-display / HomeLink rows (the
                        three web divider sections), + the SSE live pip.
   5. Tire Pressure   — FL/FR/RL/RR corner tiles (Pa→kPa→user-unit, banded tones) + the
                        overall ✓/✗/⚠ status chip.
   6. Energy & Charging— voltage/current tiles, charger-power + energy-added rows (web
                        `fmtWithUnit(raw_w,'kW')` / `(raw_wh,'kWh')` quirk reproduced
                        VERBATIM), charging-state chip, battery level, charge rate.
   7. Media & Navigation— now-playing (title/artist/source/status with playback tones) +
                        navigation (destination, distance via convertDistanceFromSI + ETA,
                        home/work/favorite place chips). Always renders; per-sub-block empty.

  Numeric pipeline ported VERBATIM from the web libs: lib/numberFormat (`fmtNumber` /
  `fmtInt` / `fmtWithUnit`, grouped, locale-aware, half-up; global precision 2),
  lib/unitConversion (`convert*FromSI` + `format*` for distance/speed/temperature/pressure;
  km/mi/ft + KPA_PER_PSI/BAR byte-identical; °unit no-space rule; per-quantity default
  precision distance 1 / speed 0 / temperature 1 / pressure 1), lib/cleanNil (Go "<nil>"
  scrubbing), and vehicle-detail/helpers `TIRE_PRESSURE_PA` Pascal bands. SI is read
  directly from the seam; conversion happens only at the render boundary (web `useUnits`).

  Note (legacy proto-name fidelity): the web nav distance flows the legacy-named
  `miles_to_arrival` field through `convertDistanceFromSI` — i.e. it is SI metres on the
  wire. Modelled as `metresToArrival` and reproduced verbatim.

